WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.339
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.639 --> 00:00:09.048
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.348 --> 00:00:15.216
Unit eight: Yes/No Questions. Today you will ask questions that have yes or no answers.

4
00:00:15.516 --> 00:00:18.006
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:22.141
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.983 --> 00:00:23.833
Do you...?.

7
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:27.468
Do you...? means a question about you.

8
00:00:28.083 --> 00:00:29.363
Do you like music?

9
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.602
Your turn. Say: Do you...?.

10
00:00:35.467 --> 00:00:36.410
Do you...?.

11
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:38.023
Does she...?.

12
00:00:39.017 --> 00:00:41.878
Does she...? means a question about one girl.

13
00:00:42.483 --> 00:00:44.053
Does she walk to school?

14
00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.070
Your turn. Say: Does she...?.

15
00:00:49.933 --> 00:00:51.016
Does she...?.

16
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:52.623
Is it...?.

17
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:56.443
Is it...? means a question about one thing.

18
00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:58.156
Is it raining?

19
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:01.309
Your turn. Say: Is it...?.

20
00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.005
Is it...?.

21
00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:06.519
Are they...?.

22
00:01:07.517 --> 00:01:10.866
Are they...? means a question about two or more people.

23
00:01:11.450 --> 00:01:12.602
Are they ready?

24
00:01:13.217 --> 00:01:15.834
Your turn. Say: Are they...?.

25
00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:19.643
Are they...?.

26
00:01:20.383 --> 00:01:21.559
Question mark.

27
00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:25.852
Question mark means the sign ? at the end of a question.

28
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.090
Put a question mark here.

29
00:01:28.683 --> 00:01:31.696
Your turn. Say: Question mark.

30
00:01:34.533 --> 00:01:35.767
Question mark.

31
00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:37.378
Answer.

32
00:01:38.383 --> 00:01:40.627
Answer means a reply to a question.

33
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:42.566
Give a short answer.

34
00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.396
Your turn. Say: Answer.

35
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:49.223
Answer.

36
00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:50.938
Yes, I do.

37
00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:54.600
Yes, I do means a short positive answer.

38
00:01:55.183 --> 00:01:57.499
Do you like tea? Yes, I do.

39
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:01.003
Your turn. Say: Yes, I do.

40
00:02:03.867 --> 00:02:04.879
Yes, I do.

41
00:02:05.617 --> 00:02:06.769
No, I don't.

42
00:02:07.783 --> 00:02:10.166
No, I don't means a short negative answer.

43
00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:13.217
Do you swim? No, I don't.

44
00:02:13.817 --> 00:02:16.713
Your turn. Say: No, I don't.

45
00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:20.579
No, I don't.

46
00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:25.134
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:25.983 --> 00:02:29.483
Visal, do you like music? Please answer in a short way.

48
00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:39.078
Yes, I do. We make yes or no questions with do or does at the start: Do you like music? Does she play the guitar?

49
00:02:40.183 --> 00:02:41.521
And with the verb be?

50
00:02:42.617 --> 00:02:52.243
We put am, is or are first: Is it raining? Are they ready? Do not add do. Are you happy? Yes, I am.

51
00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:54.943
Which answer is correct?

52
00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:07.344
Use the same helping verb. Do you swim? Yes, I do. No, I don't. Is she here? Yes, she is. No, she isn't. Finish with a question mark.

53
00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.256
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.117 --> 00:03:16.135
Grammar focus: Yes and no questions: Do and Does and Am and Is and Are.

55
00:03:16.435 --> 00:03:17.529
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:18.217 --> 00:03:19.485
Do you like music?

57
00:03:20.383 --> 00:03:21.872
Does she walk to school?

58
00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:23.854
Are they ready?

59
00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:33.414
Put do, does, am, is or are before the subject. Answer with the same helping verb: Yes, I do. No, she isn't. Finish with a question mark.

60
00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:37.789
Be careful! Don't say: Does she plays tennis?

61
00:03:39.733 --> 00:03:42.685
Say: Does she play tennis?

62
00:03:42.985 --> 00:03:44.926
Use the base verb after does.

63
00:03:45.733 --> 00:03:48.537
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:49.333 --> 00:03:50.787
Questions and Answers.

65
00:03:51.087 --> 00:03:53.438
Do you like music? Yes, I do.

66
00:03:54.433 --> 00:03:57.713
Does your teacher speak English? Yes, she does.

67
00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:01.062
Is it Monday today? No, it isn't.

68
00:04:02.067 --> 00:04:04.882
Are your friends at school? Yes, they are.

69
00:04:05.867 --> 00:04:08.040
A question ends with a question mark.

70
00:04:09.133 --> 00:04:13.123
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:13.983 --> 00:04:15.426
blank you like pizza?

72
00:04:15.726 --> 00:04:18.543
A, Do. B, Does. C, Is.

73
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.705
The answer is A: Do.

74
00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:26.257
blank she live here?

75
00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:29.410
A, Do. B, Is. C, Does.

76
00:04:32.967 --> 00:04:34.978
The answer is C: Does.

77
00:04:36.117 --> 00:04:37.910
Is it hot? blank

78
00:04:38.210 --> 00:04:42.258
A, Yes, it is.. B, Yes, it does.. C, Yes, it do..

79
00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:47.858
The answer is A: Yes, it is..

80
00:04:49.017 --> 00:04:50.691
Which question is correct?

81
00:04:50.991 --> 00:04:56.769
A, Does he plays football?. B, Does he play football?. C, Do he play football?.

82
00:05:00.333 --> 00:05:03.064
The answer is B: Does he play football?.

83
00:05:04.217 --> 00:05:07.342
According to the reading, how does a question end?

84
00:05:07.642 --> 00:05:11.772
A, with a question mark. B, with a full stop. C, with a comma.

85
00:05:15.333 --> 00:05:17.716
The answer is A: with a question mark.

86
00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:21.935
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:22.783 --> 00:05:26.339
Ask a partner a yes/no question about their daily routine.

88
00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.604
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:36.904 --> 00:05:52.971
I ask my partner: Do you wake up at six o'clock? My partner can answer: Yes, I do, or No, I don't. I start with do and use the base verb. At the end of the question, I write a question mark.

90
00:05:53.271 --> 00:05:54.957
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:55.850 --> 00:06:02.368
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and yes and no questions: do and does and am and is and are.

92
00:06:02.668 --> 00:06:06.795
Today's value is curiosity. Ask questions and find out.

93
00:06:07.095 --> 00:06:09.492
See you in Unit nine. Goodbye!

94
00:06:09.792 --> 00:06:12.479
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

